          "problem": "Let $z = 2 + \\sqrt{2} - (3 + 3 \\sqrt{2})i$, and let $c = 2 - 3i$.  Let $w$ be the result when $z$ is rotated around $c$ by $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ counter-clockwise.\n\n[asy]\nunitsize(0.6 cm);\n\npair C, W, Z;\n\nZ = (2 + sqrt(2), -3 - 3*sqrt(2));\nC = (2,-3);\nW = rotate(45,C)*(Z);\n\ndraw(Z--C--W);\n\ndot(\"$c$\", C, N);\ndot(\"$w$\", W, SE);\ndot(\"$z$\", Z, S);\nlabel(\"$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\", C + (0.6,-1));\n[/asy]\n\nFind $w.$",
          "solution": "Rotating by $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ counter-clockwise corresponds to the complex number\n\\[e^{\\pi i/4} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\]Hence,\n\\[w - c = \\left( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\right) (z - c),\\]so\n\\begin{align*}\nw &= \\left( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\right) (z - c) + c \\\\\n&= \\left( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\right) (\\sqrt{2} - 3i \\sqrt{2}) + 2 - 3i \\\\\n&= (4 - 2i) + 2 - 3i \\\\\n&= \\boxed{6 - 5i}.\n\\end{align*}",
          "answer": "6 - 5i",
          "subject": "Precalculus",
          "level": 5,
          "unique_id": "test/precalculus/990.json",
          "model_output": "To solve for $w$, we first need to understand the rotation of $z$ around $c$ by $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ counter-clockwise. The rotation of a complex number $z$ around another complex number $c$ by an angle $\\theta$ counter-clockwise can be represented by the formula:\n\\[ w = c + (z - c)e^{i\\theta} \\]\n\nGiven:\n- $z = 2 + \\sqrt{2} - (3 + 3\\sqrt{2})i$\n- $c = 2 - 3i$\n- $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$\n\nFirst, calculate $z - c$:\n\\[ z - c = (2 + \\sqrt{2} - (3 + 3\\sqrt{2})i) - (2 - 3i) \\]\n\\[ z - c = \\sqrt{2} - 3i \\]\n\nNext, calculate $e^{i\\theta}$:\n\\[ e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) + i\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\]\n\\[ e^{i\\theta} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + i\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\]\n\nNow, apply the rotation formula:\n\\[ w = c + (z - c)e^{i\\theta} \\]\n\\[ w = (2 - 3i) + (\\sqrt{2} - 3i)\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + i\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\]\n\\[ w = (2 - 3i) + \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sqrt{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot3i\\right) + \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot3i\\sqrt{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot3i\\right) \\]\n\\[ w = (2 - 3i) + (1 - 3i) + (3i - 3i) \\]\n\\[ w = (2 - 3i) + (1 - 3i) \\]\n\\[ w = 3 - 6i \\]\n\nThus, the result of the rotation is:\n\\[ \\boxed{w = 3 - 6i} \\]",
