          "model_output": "The graph of $y = a \\sin (bx + c) + d$ is a sine wave with amplitude $a$, period $\\frac{2\\pi}{b}$, and vertical shift $d$.\n\nThe period of the graph is $\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$, so we have $\\frac{2\\pi}{b} = \\frac{2\\pi}{3}$, which implies $b = 3$.\n\nThe amplitude of the graph is $2$, so we have $a = 2$.\n\nThe vertical shift of the graph is $1$, so we have $d = 1$.\n\nThe graph is shifted to the right by $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$, so we have $c = \\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $c$ is $\\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}$.",
          "model_answer": "\\frac{\\pi}{6}"
