          "unique_id": "test/precalculus/1146.json",
          "model_output": "To find the value of $d$ in the given equation, we can use the fact that the equation holds for all angles $x$. This implies that the coefficients of the sine terms must be equal on both sides of the equation.\n\nWe can rewrite the equation as:\n\\[(\\sin x)^7 = a \\sin 7x + b \\sin 5x + c \\sin 3x + d \\sin x\\]\n\nNow, we can use the sum-to-product identities to rewrite the equation as:\n\\[(\\sin x)^7 = \\sin x (a \\sin 6x + b \\sin 4x + c \\sin 2x + d \\sin x)\\]\n\nSince the equation holds for all angles $x$, the coefficients of the sine terms must be equal on both sides. Therefore, we have:\n\\[a = d\\]\n\nSo, the value of $d$ is $\\boxed{a}$.",
          "model_answer": "a"
