          "model_output": "Let the original side length of the square be $s$. The area of the square is $s^2$.\n\nWhen the length of one side of the square is decreased by $40\\%$, the new length is $0.6s$. When the length of the other side of the square is increased by $50\\%$, the new length is $1.5s$.\n\nThe new dimensions of the rectangle are $0.6s$ and $1.5s$. The area of the rectangle is $(0.6s)(1.5s) = 0.9s^2$.\n\nThe percent decrease in the area of the square is:\n\\[\n\\frac{s^2 - 0.9s^2}{s^2} \\times 100\\% = \\frac{0.1s^2}{s^2} \\times 100\\% = 10\\%\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the square's area decreases by $\\boxed{10\\%}$.",
