          "unique_id": "test/counting_and_probability/377.json",
          "model_output": "To find the probability that exactly 4 out of 7 islands have treasure, we can use the binomial probability formula. The formula is:\n\n\\[ P(X = k) = \\binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k} \\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( n \\) is the number of trials (in this case, 7 islands),\n- \\( k \\) is the number of successful trials (in this case, 4 islands with treasure),\n- \\( p \\) is the probability of success on a single trial (in this case, \\( \\frac{1}{5} \\)),\n- \\( \\binom{n}{k} \\) is the binomial coefficient, calculated as \\( \\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \\).\n\nPlugging in the values:\n\n\\[ P(X = 4) = \\binom{7}{4} \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^4 \\left(1 - \\frac{1}{5}\\right)^{7-4} \\]\n\n\\[ P(X = 4) = \\binom{7}{4} \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^4 \\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^3 \\]\n\n\\[ P(X = 4) = \\binom{7}{4} \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^4 \\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^3 \\]\n\n\\[ P(X = 4) = \\frac{7!}{4!3!} \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^4 \\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^3 \\]\n\n\\[ P(X = 4) = \\frac{7 \\times 6 \\times 5}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^4 \\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^3 \\]\n\n\\[ P(X = 4) = 35 \\left(\\frac{1}{625}\\right) \\left(\\frac{64}{125}\\right) \\]\n\n\\[ P(X = 4) = 35 \\left(\\frac{64}{78125}\\right) \\]\n\n\\[ P(X = 4) = \\frac{2240}{78125} \\]\n\n\\[ P(X = 4) = \\frac{2240}{78125} \\]\n\n\\[ P(X = 4) = \\boxed{\\frac{2240}{78125}} \\]",
