          "unique_id": "test/precalculus/34.json",
          "model_output": "The projection of a vector $\\mathbf{a}$ onto another vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is given by the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\nGiven that the projection of $\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ y \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}$ onto $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ is $\\frac{5}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$, we can set up the following equation:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ y \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}}{\\|\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\|^2} = \\frac{5}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nFirst, calculate the dot product:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ y \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} = 2 \\cdot 1 + y \\cdot (-2) + (-5) \\cdot 1 = 2 - 2y - 5 = -3 - 2y\n\\]\nNext, calculate the magnitude squared of $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$:\n\\[\n\\|\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\|^2 = 1^2 + (-2)^2 + 1^2 = 1 + 4 + 1 = 6\n\\]\nSubstitute these values into the projection formula:\n\\[\n\\frac{-3 - 2y}{6} = \\frac{5}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[\n\\frac{-3 - 2y}{6} = \\frac{5}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nMultiply both sides by 6 to clear the fraction:\n\\[\n-3 - 2y = 5 \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nExpand the right-hand side:\n\\[\n-3 - 2y = \\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nEquating the corresponding components, we get:\n\\[\n-3 - 2y = 5 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad -3 - 2y = -10 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad -3 - 2y = 5\n\\]\nSolving the first equation:\n\\[\n-3 - 2y = 5 \\implies -2y = 8 \\implies y = -4\n\\]\nThus, the value of $y$ is $\\boxed{-4}$.",
