          "model_output": "To solve the given equation, we start by simplifying each term:\n\n1. For the first term:\n\\[\n\\frac{(x+1)(x-3)}{5(x+2)(x-4)} = \\frac{x^2 - 2x - 3}{5(x+2)(x-4)} = \\frac{x^2 - 2x - 3}{5(x^2 - 2x - 8)}\n\\]\n\n2. For the second term:\n\\[\n\\frac{(x+3)(x-5)}{9(x+4)(x-6)} = \\frac{x^2 - 2x - 15}{9(x+4)(x-6)} = \\frac{x^2 - 2x - 15}{9(x^2 - 2x - 24)}\n\\]\n\n3. For the third term:\n\\[\n\\frac{2(x+5)(x-7)}{13(x+6)(x-8)} = \\frac{2(x^2 - 2x - 35)}{13(x^2 - 2x - 48)} = \\frac{2(x^2 - 2x - 35)}{13(x^2 - 2x - 48)}\n\\]\n\nNow, we combine these terms:\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2 - 2x - 3}{5(x^2 - 2x - 8)} + \\frac{x^2 - 2x - 15}{9(x^2 - 2x - 24)} - \\frac{2(x^2 - 2x - 35)}{13(x^2 - 2x - 48)} = \\frac{92}{585}\n\\]\n\nTo combine these fractions, we find a common denominator, which is $585(x^2 - 2x - 8)(x^2 - 2x - 24)(x^2 - 2x - 48)$. After simplifying, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{585(x^2 - 2x - 35) + 65(x^2 - 2x - 15) - 90(x^2 - 2x - 8)}{585(x^2 - 2x - 8)(x^2 - 2x - 24)(x^2 - 2x - 48)} = \\frac{92}{585}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the numerator:\n\\[\n585(x^2 - 2x - 35) + 65(x^2 - 2x - 15) - 90(x^2 - 2x - 8) = 585x^2 - 1170x - 2025 + 1325x - 1050 - 870x + 1440 - 585x^2 + 1170x + 1440 = -2025 + 1440 = -585\n\\]\n\nThus, the equation simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{-585}{585(x^2 - 2x - 8)(x^2 - 2x - 24)(x^2 - 2x - 48)} = \\frac{92}{585}\n\\]\n\nMultiplying both sides by $585(x^2 - 2x - 8)(x^2 - 2x - 24)(x^2 - 2x - 48)$:\n\\[\n-585 = 92(x^2 - 2x - 8)(x^2 - 2x - 24)(x^2 - 2x - 48)\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n(x^2 - 2x - 8)(x^2 - 2x - 24)(x^2 - 2x - 48) = -\\frac{585}{92}\n\\]\n\nSince the left side is a product of three quadratic terms, it is always non-negative. Therefore, the right side must also be non-negative, which implies:\n\\[\n-\\frac{585}{92} \\geq 0\n\\]\n\nThis is not possible, so there are no real solutions.\n\nConclusion:\nThe equation has no real roots.\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{No real roots}}\n\\]",
