          "unique_id": "test/precalculus/44.json",
          "model_output": "We start by simplifying the given expression using trigonometric identities:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}{\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}.\n\\]\nUsing the cosine of the sum of two angles, we can rewrite the numerator and denominator:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos(5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) + \\cos(35^\\circ + 50^\\circ)}{\\sin(5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) - \\sin(35^\\circ + 50^\\circ)}.\n\\]\nSimplifying further, we get:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ}.\n\\]\nUsing the cosine of the sum of two angles, we can rewrite the numerator and denominator:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos(25^\\circ + 85^\\circ)}{\\sin(25^\\circ + 85^\\circ)}.\n\\]\nSimplifying further, we get:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 110^\\circ}{\\sin 110^\\circ}.\n\\]\nSince $\\tan 110^\\circ = \\tan (180^\\circ - 70^\\circ) = -\\tan 70^\\circ$, we have:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = -\\tan 70^\\circ.\n\\]\nTherefore, the least positive angle $\\theta$ for which $\\tan \\theta = -\\tan 70^\\circ$ is $\\boxed{70^\\circ}$.",
