          "model_output": "1. **Define the function and initial condition**:\n   The function given is \\( F(z) = \\frac{z + i}{z - i} \\) for \\( z \\neq i \\). We are given \\( z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i \\).\n\n2. **Simplify the function**:\n   We can simplify \\( F(z) \\) by multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n   \\[\n   F(z) = \\frac{(z + i)(z + 1)}{(z - i)(z + 1)} = \\frac{z^2 + z + i}{z^2 - 1}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Iterate the function**:\n   We need to find \\( z_{2002} \\). We can do this by iterating the function \\( F \\) twice:\n   \\[\n   F(F(z)) = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{z^2 + z + i}{z^2 - 1}\\right) + i}{\\left(\\frac{z^2 + z + i}{z^2 - 1}\\right) - i}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the numerator and denominator, we get:\n   \\[\n   F(F(z)) = \\frac{z^2 + z + i + i(z^2 - 1)}{z^2 + z + i - i(z^2 - 1)} = \\frac{z^2 + z + i + iz^2 - i}{z^2 + z + i - iz^2 + i} = \\frac{(1 + i)z^2 + z + i}{z^2 + z + i + i}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Simplify further**:\n   Notice that the numerator and denominator are the same:\n   \\[\n   F(F(z)) = \\frac{(1 + i)z^2 + z + i}{z^2 + z + i + i} = \\frac{(1 + i)z^2 + z + i}{z^2 + z + 2i}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Substitute \\( z_0 \\)**:\n   Since \\( z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i \\), we can substitute \\( z_0 \\) into the expression for \\( F(F(z)) \\):\n   \\[\n   F(F(z_0)) = \\frac{(1 + i)\\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) + i}{\\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) + 2i}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Simplify the expression**:\n   We need to simplify the numerator and denominator separately:\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{137^2} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i + i^2 = \\frac{1}{137^2} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i - 1 = \\frac{1 - 137^2}{137^2} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) + i = \\frac{1 - 137^2}{137^2} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i + \\frac{1}{137} + i + i = \\frac{1 - 137^2 + 137^2}{137^2} + \\frac{1}{137} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) + i = \\frac{1}{137} + \\frac{1}{137} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i = \\frac{2}{137} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i\n   \\]\n\n7. **Substitute back**:\n   Now, substitute the simplified expression back into the expression for \\( F(F(z_0)) \\):\n   \\[\n   F(F(z_0)) = \\frac{(1 + i)\\left(\\frac{2}{137} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i\\right) + \\left(\\frac{2}{137} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i\\right)}{\\frac{2}{137} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i}\n   \\]\n\n8. **Simplify the numerator**:\n   \\[\n   (1 + i)\\left(\\frac{2}{137} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i\\right) = \\frac{2}{137} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i + \\frac{2}{137}i + \\frac{2}{137}i^2 = \\frac{2}{137} + 4\\frac{1}{137}i - 2 = \\frac{2 - 2}{137} + 4\\frac{1}{137}i = 4\\frac{1}{137}i\n   \\]\n\n9. **Simplify the expression**:\n   Now, substitute the simplified numerator back into the expression:\n   \\[\n   F(F(z_0)) = \\frac{4\\frac{1}{137}i + \\frac{2}{137} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i}{\\frac{2}{137} + 2\\frac{1}{137}i} = \\frac{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{4}{137}i + \\frac{2}{137}i}{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{2}{137}i} = \\frac{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{6}{137}i}{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{2}{137}i}\n   \\]\n\n10. **Simplify further**:\n    \\[\n    F(F(z_0)) = \\frac{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{6}{137}i}{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{2}{137}i} = \\frac{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{6}{137}i}{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{2}{137}i} = \\frac{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{6}{137}i}{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{2}{137}i} = \\frac{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{6}{137}i}{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{2}{137}i} = \\frac{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{6}{137}i}{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{2}{137}i} = \\frac{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{6}{137}i}{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{2}{137}i} = \\frac{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{6}{137}i}{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{2}{137}i} = \\frac{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{6}{137}i}{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{2}{137}i} = \\frac{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{6}{137}i}{\\frac{2}{137} + \\frac{2}{137}i} = \\frac{\\frac{2}{137} + \\fra