          "unique_id": "test/precalculus/477.json",
          "model_output": "To find the area of triangle $OAB$, we can use the formula for the area of a triangle given by two vectors $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ originating from the same point:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} \\right|\n\\]\nHere, $\\mathbf{u} = \\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{v} = \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$.\n\nFirst, we calculate the cross product $\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}$:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} \\times \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} (2)(1) - (3)(-2) \\\\ (3)(-3) - (1)(1) \\\\ (1)(-2) - (2)(-3) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 + 6 \\\\ -9 - 1 \\\\ -2 + 6 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the magnitude of the cross product:\n\\[\n\\left| \\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} \\right| = \\sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \\sqrt{180} = 6\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate the area of triangle $OAB$:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6\\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of triangle $OAB$ is $\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}$.",
