          "unique_id": "test/geometry/880.json",
          "model_output": "1. **Identify the dimensions of the room and the positions of the gecko and the fly:**\n   - The room is 12 feet long, 10 feet wide, and 8 feet tall.\n   - The gecko is on a side wall, one foot from the ceiling and one foot from the back wall.\n   - The fly is on the opposite side wall, one foot from the floor and one foot from the front wall.\n\n2. **Calculate the distance from the gecko to the fly:**\n   - The gecko is on a side wall, so the distance from the gecko to the fly is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs of length 12 feet (length of the side wall) and 8 feet (height of the room).\n   - Using the Pythagorean theorem, the distance \\(d\\) is:\n     \\[\n     d = \\sqrt{12^2 + 8^2} = \\sqrt{144 + 64} = \\sqrt{208} = 4\\sqrt{13}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   - The shortest path the gecko can take to reach the fly is \\(4\\sqrt{13}\\) feet.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4\\sqrt{13}}\n\\]",
          "model_answer": "4\\sqrt{13}"
