          "unique_id": "test/prealgebra/1272.json",
          "model_output": "To find out how much of the pie Louis and Jack eat altogether, we need to add the fractions of the pie they each eat. Louis eats $\\frac{1}{5}$ of the pie, and Jack eats $\\frac{2}{3}$ of the pie. To add these fractions, we need to find a common denominator. The least common multiple of 5 and 3 is 15, so we convert both fractions to have a denominator of 15.\n\nFor Louis:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5} = \\frac{1 \\times 3}{5 \\times 3} = \\frac{3}{15}\n\\]\n\nFor Jack:\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{2 \\times 5}{3 \\times 5} = \\frac{10}{15}\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the fractions:\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{15} + \\frac{10}{15} = \\frac{3 + 10}{15} = \\frac{13}{15}\n\\]\n\nSo, Louis and Jack together eat $\\boxed{\\frac{13}{15}}$ of the pie.",
