          "model_output": "To solve this problem, we need to consider the different combinations of dishes that Yann and Camille can order, given that they refuse to order the same dish. Since there are 10 items on the menu, Yann can choose any of the 10 dishes, and then Camille can choose any of the remaining 9 dishes.\n\nThe total number of different combinations of meals that Yann and Camille can order is calculated by multiplying the number of choices Yann has by the number of choices Camille has. This is because for each choice Yann makes, there are 9 choices Camille can make.\n\nSo, the total number of different combinations is:\n\\[ 10 \\times 9 = 90 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of different combinations of meals that Yann and Camille can order is \\(\\boxed{90}\\).",
