          "model_output": "Let's denote the number of sides of the polygon as \\( n \\). The sum of the interior angles of a polygon with \\( n \\) sides is given by the formula \\( (n-2) \\times 180^{\\circ} \\).\n\nAccording to the problem, the sum of all but one of the interior angles is \\( 1070^{\\circ} \\). This means that the sum of the remaining \\( n-1 \\) angles is \\( 1070^{\\circ} \\).\n\nSo, we can write the equation:\n\\[\n(n-2) \\times 180^{\\circ} = 1070^{\\circ} + (n-1) \\times 180^{\\circ}\n\\]\n\nNow, let's solve for \\( n \\):\n\\[\n(n-2) \\times 180^{\\circ} = 1070^{\\circ} + (n-1) \\times 180^{\\circ}\n\\]\n\\[\n(n-2) \\times 180^{\\circ} - (n-1) \\times 180^{\\circ} = 1070^{\\circ}\n\\]\n\\[\n180^{\\circ} \\times (n-2 - n + 1) = 1070^{\\circ}\n\\]\n\\[\n180^{\\circ} \\times (-1) = 1070^{\\circ}\n\\]\n\\[\n-180^{\\circ} = 1070^{\\circ}\n\\]\n\nThis equation is not possible, which means there is no solution for \\( n \\) that satisfies the given conditions. Therefore, there is no convex polygon with the sum of all but one of its interior angles being \\( 1070^{\\circ} \\).\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{No solution}}\\).",
