          "unique_id": "test/counting_and_probability/1009.json",
          "model_output": "To solve this problem, we need to consider the different combinations of cookies that can be selected from the tray. Since there are at least six of each type of cookie, we can start by selecting the minimum number of each type of cookie.\n\n1. **Selecting the minimum number of each type of cookie:**\n   - We need to select at least 6 chocolate chip cookies.\n   - We need to select at least 6 oatmeal cookies.\n   - We need to select at least 6 peanut butter cookies.\n\n2. **Calculating the number of ways to select the minimum number of each type of cookie:**\n   - The number of ways to select 6 chocolate chip cookies from 6 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{6}{6} = 1 \\).\n   - The number of ways to select 6 oatmeal cookies from 6 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{6}{6} = 1 \\).\n   - The number of ways to select 6 peanut butter cookies from 6 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{6}{6} = 1 \\).\n\n3. **Calculating the total number of ways to select the minimum number of each type of cookie:**\n   - Since the selections of each type of cookie are independent, we multiply the number of ways to select each type of cookie:\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 1 \\times 1 = 1\n   \\]\n\n4. **Selecting the remaining cookies:**\n   - After selecting the minimum number of each type of cookie, we have 2 cookies left to select.\n   - We need to select 2 cookies from the remaining 2 types of cookies (oatmeal and peanut butter).\n\n5. **Calculating the number of ways to select the remaining cookies:**\n   - The number of ways to select 2 oatmeal cookies from 2 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{2}{2} = 1 \\).\n   - The number of ways to select 2 peanut butter cookies from 2 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{2}{2} = 1 \\).\n\n6. **Calculating the total number of ways to select the remaining cookies:**\n   - Since the selections of the remaining cookies are independent, we multiply the number of ways to select each type of cookie:\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 1 = 1\n   \\]\n\n7. **Calculating the total number of different assortments of six cookies:**\n   - We multiply the number of ways to select the minimum number of each type of cookie by the number of ways to select the remaining cookies:\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 1 = 1\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of different assortments of six cookies that can be selected is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
