          "model_output": "To compute the product of the number $5+\\sqrt{3}$ and its radical conjugate, we first need to find the radical conjugate of $5+\\sqrt{3}$. The radical conjugate of a number is obtained by changing the sign of the radical part. Therefore, the radical conjugate of $5+\\sqrt{3}$ is $5-\\sqrt{3}$.\n\nNow, we multiply the two numbers:\n\\[\n(5+\\sqrt{3})(5-\\sqrt{3})\n\\]\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula, which states that $(a+b)(a-b) = a^2 - b^2$, we can simplify the expression:\n\\[\n(5+\\sqrt{3})(5-\\sqrt{3}) = 5^2 - (\\sqrt{3})^2\n\\]\n\nCalculating the squares, we get:\n\\[\n5^2 = 25 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad (\\sqrt{3})^2 = 3\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these values back into the expression, we have:\n\\[\n25 - 3 = 22\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the product of the number $5+\\sqrt{3}$ and its radical conjugate is $\\boxed{22}$.",
