          "model_output": "To find the angle $\\angle ABC$, we can use the dot product formula for vectors. First, we need to find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{BA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{BC}$.\n\n1. Calculate $\\overrightarrow{BA}$:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{BA} = A - B = (1 - 3, -11 - (-4), 2 - 1) = (-2, -7, 1)\n\\]\n\n2. Calculate $\\overrightarrow{BC}$:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{BC} = C - B = (-2 - 3, 1 - (-4), -1 - 1) = (-5, 5, -2)\n\\]\n\n3. Calculate the dot product $\\overrightarrow{BA} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{BC}$:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{BA} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{BC} = (-2)(-5) + (-7)(5) + (1)(-2) = 10 - 35 - 2 = -27\n\\]\n\n4. Calculate the magnitudes of $\\overrightarrow{BA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{BC}$:\n\\[\n|\\overrightarrow{BA}| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-7)^2 + 1^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 49 + 1} = \\sqrt{54} = 3\\sqrt{6}\n\\]\n\\[\n|\\overrightarrow{BC}| = \\sqrt{(-5)^2 + 5^2 + (-2)^2} = \\sqrt{25 + 25 + 4} = \\sqrt{54} = 3\\sqrt{6}\n\\]\n\n5. Calculate the cosine of the angle $\\cos \\theta$:\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\overrightarrow{BA} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{BC}}{|\\overrightarrow{BA}| |\\overrightarrow{BC}|} = \\frac{-27}{3\\sqrt{6} \\cdot 3\\sqrt{6}} = \\frac{-27}{54} = -\\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\n6. Calculate the angle $\\theta$:\n\\[\n\\theta = \\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = 120^\\circ\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the angle $\\angle ABC$ is $\\boxed{120^\\circ}$.",
