          "unique_id": "test/geometry/483.json",
          "model_output": "Let's denote the measure of an interior angle as \\( I \\) and the measure of an exterior angle as \\( E \\). According to the problem, we have the relationship:\n\n\\[ I = 6.5E \\]\n\nIn a regular polygon, the sum of the interior angles is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ \\]\n\nwhere \\( n \\) is the number of sides. Since the sum of the interior angles of a polygon is also equal to the sum of the exterior angles, we can write:\n\n\\[ (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ = n \\times 180^\\circ \\]\n\nNow, we can solve for \\( n \\) by dividing both sides of the equation by \\( 180^\\circ \\):\n\n\\[ n - 2 = n \\]\n\nSubtracting \\( n \\) from both sides, we get:\n\n\\[ -2 = 0 \\]\n\nThis equation is not possible, which means there is no regular polygon that satisfies the given condition. Therefore, the problem as stated does not have a solution.",
          "model_answer": ""
