          "level": 2,
          "unique_id": "test/algebra/524.json",
          "model_output": "The sequence of odd numbers is an arithmetic sequence with a common difference of 2. To find the 2003rd term, we can use the formula for the nth term of an arithmetic sequence:\n\na_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\n\nwhere a_n is the nth term, a_1 is the first term, n is the term number, and d is the common difference.\n\nIn this case, a_1 = 1 (the first term), n = 2003 (the term number), and d = 2 (the common difference).\n\nPlugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\na_2003 = 1 + (2003-1)2\na_2003 = 1 + 2002*2\na_2003 = 1 + 4004\na_2003 = 4005\n\nTherefore, the 2003rd term of the sequence of odd numbers is $\\boxed{4005}$.",
