          "problem": "Find the value of $r$ such that $$\\frac{6r^2 -19r - 7}{2r-7} = 4r-3.$$",
          "solution": "Factoring the quadratic on the left gives $$\\frac{(2r-7)(3r+1)}{2r-7} = 4r-3.$$Canceling the common factor on the left gives $3r + 1 = 4r - 3$.  Solving this equation gives $r = \\boxed{4}$.",
          "answer": "4",
          "subject": "Algebra",
          "level": 3,
          "unique_id": "test/algebra/634.json",
          "model_output": "To solve the equation $\\frac{6r^2 -19r - 7}{2r-7} = 4r-3$, we start by cross-multiplying to eliminate the fraction:\n\n\\[\n6r^2 - 19r - 7 = (4r - 3)(2r - 7)\n\\]\n\nExpanding the right-hand side, we get:\n\n\\[\n6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 28r - 6r + 21\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the right-hand side, we have:\n\n\\[\n6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 34r + 21\n\\]\n\nNext, we move all terms to one side of the equation to set it to zero:\n\n\\[\n6r^2 - 19r - 7 - 8r^2 + 34r - 21 = 0\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n-2r^2 + 15r - 28 = 0\n\\]\n\nMultiplying through by $-1$ to simplify, we have:\n\n\\[\n2r^2 - 15r + 28 = 0\n\\]\n\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula, $r = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}$, where $a = 2$, $b = -15$, and $c = 28$:\n\n\\[\nr = \\frac{-(-15) \\pm \\sqrt{(-15)^2 - 4 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 28}}{2 \\cdot 2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nr = \\frac{15 \\pm \\sqrt{225 - 224}}{4}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nr = \\frac{15 \\pm \\sqrt{1}}{4}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nr = \\frac{15 \\pm 1}{4}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us two possible solutions:\n\n\\[\nr = \\frac{15 + 1}{4} = \\frac{16}{4} = 4\n\\]\n\n\\[\nr = \\frac{15 - 1}{4} = \\frac{14}{4} = \\frac{7}{2}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $r = 4$ and $r = \\frac{7}{2}$.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{r = 4 \\text{ or } r = \\frac{7}{2}}\n\\]",
          "model_answer": "r = 4 \\text{ or } r = \\frac{7}{2}"
