          "level": 4,
          "unique_id": "test/algebra/2257.json",
          "model_output": "To solve the equation $\\frac{\\sqrt{2x}}{\\sqrt{3x-1}}=\\frac{3}{2}$, we start by cross-multiplying to eliminate the fractions:\n\n\\[\n2\\sqrt{2x} = 3\\sqrt{3x-1}\n\\]\n\nNext, we square both sides to remove the square roots:\n\n\\[\n(2\\sqrt{2x})^2 = (3\\sqrt{3x-1})^2\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 2x = 9 \\cdot (3x - 1)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n8x = 27x - 9\n\\]\n\nRearranging the terms to isolate $x$, we get:\n\n\\[\n27x - 8x = 9\n\\]\n\n\\[\n19x = 9\n\\]\n\nFinally, solving for $x$ gives:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{9}{19}\n\\]\n\nThus, the solution to the equation is $\\boxed{\\frac{9}{19}}$.",
