          "model_output": "To find the degree of the polynomial $p(x)$, we need to analyze the highest degree term in the expression.\n\n1. **Identify the highest degree term in each fraction:**\n   - The highest degree term in $\\frac{(x - b)(x - c)}{(a - b)(a - c)}$ is $x^2$.\n   - The highest degree term in $\\frac{(x - a)(x - c)}{(b - a)(b - c)}$ is $x^2$.\n   - The highest degree term in $\\frac{(x - a)(x - b)}{(c - a)(c - b)}$ is $x^2$.\n\n2. **Combine the highest degree terms:**\n   - Since all three fractions have the same highest degree term $x^2$, we can combine them:\n     \\[\n     p(x) = \\frac{x^2}{1} + \\frac{x^2}{1} + \\frac{x^2}{1} = 3x^2\n     \\]\n\n3. **Determine the degree of the polynomial:**\n   - The highest degree term in $3x^2$ is $x^2$.\n   - Therefore, the degree of the polynomial $p(x)$ is $\\boxed{2}$.",
