          "model_output": "To write the expression as a single fraction, we need to find a common denominator for the two fractions. The common denominator for 5 and 4 is 20. We can rewrite the expression as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4+6a}{5}-\\frac{1+3a}{4} = \\frac{4(4+6a)}{20} - \\frac{5(1+3a)}{20}\n\\]\n\nNow, we can simplify the expression by combining the numerators:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4(4+6a)}{20} - \\frac{5(1+3a)}{20} = \\frac{16 + 24a - 5 - 15a}{20}\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms in the numerator, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{16 + 24a - 5 - 15a}{20} = \\frac{11 + 9a}{20}\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression can be written as a single fraction:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{11 + 9a}{20}}\n\\]",
