          "model_output": "To solve the equation $|x-4| -10 = 2$, we first isolate the absolute value expression by adding 10 to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ |x-4| - 10 + 10 = 2 + 10 \\]\n\\[ |x-4| = 12 \\]\n\nNow, we consider the two cases for the absolute value equation:\n\n1. **Case 1: $x-4 \\geq 0$**\n   \\[ x-4 = 12 \\]\n   \\[ x = 12 + 4 \\]\n   \\[ x = 16 \\]\n\n2. **Case 2: $x-4 < 0$**\n   \\[ -(x-4) = 12 \\]\n   \\[ -x + 4 = 12 \\]\n   \\[ -x = 12 - 4 \\]\n   \\[ -x = 8 \\]\n   \\[ x = -8 \\]\n\nThe possible values of $x$ are $16$ and $-8$. To find the product of these values, we multiply them together:\n\n\\[ 16 \\times (-8) = -128 \\]\n\nThus, the product of all possible values of $x$ is $\\boxed{-128}$.",
