          "model_output": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the length of the hallway based on the given information about the robot's speed and the time it takes to travel the hallway.\n\n1. **Calculate the speed of the robot:**\n   The robot travels 1 kilometer in 2.5 hours. To find the speed in meters per hour (m/h), we use the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Speed} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Time}}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the given values:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Speed} = \\frac{1000 \\text{ meters}}{2.5 \\text{ hours}} = 400 \\text{ m/h}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Convert the time to seconds:**\n   The robot takes 90 seconds to travel the length of the hallway. To find the length in meters, we use the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Length} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the speed and time:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Length} = 400 \\text{ m/h} \\times 90 \\text{ seconds} = 36000 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the length of the hallway is $\\boxed{36000}$ meters.",
