          "model_output": "To find the value of $b$, we start by evaluating $f(q(1))$.\n\nFirst, we substitute $q(1)$ into the function $f(x)$:\n\\[\nf(q(1)) = f(b \\cdot 1 + 1) = f(b + 1)\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute $b + 1$ into the function $f(x)$:\n\\[\nf(b + 1) = (b + 1) - 3\n\\]\n\nWe are given that $f(q(1)) = -3$, so we set the expression equal to $-3$:\n\\[\n(b + 1) - 3 = -3\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the equation, we get:\n\\[\nb + 1 - 3 = -3\n\\]\n\\[\nb - 2 = -3\n\\]\n\nAdding $2$ to both sides of the equation, we find:\n\\[\nb = -3 + 2\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of $b$ is $\\boxed{-1}$.",
