          "unique_id": "test/prealgebra/1973.json",
          "model_output": "To convert the bicycle's speed from feet per minute to inches per second, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the speed from feet per minute to feet per second.\n2. Convert the speed from feet per second to inches per second.\n\nStep 1: Convert the speed from feet per minute to feet per second.\n\nThe speed of the bicycle is 20 feet per minute. To convert this to feet per second, we need to divide by 60 (since there are 60 seconds in a minute).\n\n20 feet per minute ÷ 60 seconds per minute = 1/3 feet per second\n\nStep 2: Convert the speed from feet per second to inches per second.\n\nWe know that 1 foot is equal to 12 inches. Therefore, 1 foot per second is equal to 12 inches per second.\n\n1/3 feet per second ÷ 12 inches per foot = 1/36 inches per second\n\nSo, the bicycle's speed expressed in inches per second is $\\boxed{1/36}$  inches per second.",
