          "unique_id": "test/precalculus/96.json",
          "model_output": "The direction vector of the line is $\\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix}.$\nSince the direction vector is parallel to the line, it must be a scalar multiple of $\\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$\nTherefore, we have $\\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix} = k \\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ for some scalar $k.$\nThis gives us the system of equations $-7 = -7k$ and $b = k.$\nSolving the first equation, we find $k = 1.$\nSubstituting this value into the second equation, we find $b = 1.$\nTherefore, the value of $b$ is $\\boxed{1}.$\nThe answer is: 1",
