          "model_output": "To solve the problem, we need to find the value of $\\frac{-3+4i}{1+2i}$.\n\nFirst, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator, which is $1-2i$. This gives us:\n\n$$\\frac{-3+4i}{1+2i} \\cdot \\frac{1-2i}{1-2i} = \\frac{(-3+4i)(1-2i)}{(1+2i)(1-2i)}.$$\n\nExpanding the numerator and denominator, we get:\n\n$$\\frac{-3+4i}{1+2i} = \\frac{-3(1) + (-3)(-2i) + 4i(1) + 4i(-2i)}{1(1) + 1(2i) + 2i(1) + 2i(-2i)}.$$\n\nSimplifying the numerator and denominator, we have:\n\n$$\\frac{-3+4i}{1+2i} = \\frac{-3 + 8i + 4i - 8i^2}{1 + 2i + 2i - 4i^2}.$$\n\nSince $i^2 = -1$, we can substitute this value into the expression:\n\n$$\\frac{-3+4i}{1+2i} = \\frac{-3 + 8i + 4i + 8}{1 + 4i + 2i + 4}.$$\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n$$\\frac{-3+4i}{1+2i} = \\frac{11 + 12i}{5 + 6i}.$$\n\nNow, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator, which is $5-6i$:\n\n$$\\frac{11 + 12i}{5 + 6i} \\cdot \\frac{5-6i}{5-6i} = \\frac{(11+12i)(5-6i)}{(5+6i)(5-6i)}.$$\n\nExpanding the numerator and denominator, we get:\n\n$$\\frac{11(5) + 11(-6i) + 12i(5) + 12i(-6i)}{(5)(5) + (5)(6i) + (6i)(5) + (6i)(6i)}.$$\n\nSimplifying the numerator and denominator, we have:\n\n$$\\frac{55 - 66i + 60i - 72i^2}{25 + 30i + 30i - 36i^2}.$$\n\nSince $i^2 = -1$, we can substitute this value into the expression:\n\n$$\\frac{55 - 66i + 60i + 72}{25 + 60i - 36 + 72i}.$$\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n$$\\frac{55 + 12i}{49 + 132i}.$$\n\nNow, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator, which is $49-132i$:\n\n$$\\frac{55 + 12i}{49 + 132i} \\cdot \\frac{49-132i}{49-132i} = \\frac{(55+12i)(49-132i)}{(49+132i)(49-132i)}.$$\n\nExpanding the numerator and denominator, we get:\n\n$$\\frac{55(49) + 55(-132i) + 12i(49) + 12i(-132i)}{49(49) + 132i(49) + 132i(49) - 132i(132i)}.$$\n\nSimplifying the numerator and denominator, we have:\n\n$$\\frac{2755 - 7260i + 588i - 1584i^2}{2401 + 6348i + 6348i - 1728i^2}.$$\n\nSince $i^2 = -1$, we can substitute this value into the expression:\n\n$$\\frac{2755 - 7260i + 588i + 1584}{2401 + 12696i + 6348i + 1728}.$$\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n$$\\frac{2755 + 588i}{2449 + 7644i}.$$\n\nNow, we divide both the real and imaginary parts by the denominator:\n\n$$\\frac{2755 + 588i}{2449 + 7644i} = \\frac{2755}{2449} + \\frac{588}{7644}i.$$\n\nSimplifying the fractions, we get:\n\n$$\\frac{2755}{2449} = \\frac{55}{49} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\frac{588}{7644} = \\frac{1}{13}.$$\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\n$$\\boxed{\\frac{55}{49} - \\frac{1}{13}i}.$$",
