          "model_output": "To solve the inequality \\(\\frac{|x^2 - 81|}{x^2 - 36x} < 0\\), we need to consider the numerator and denominator separately and analyze their signs.\n\n1. **Analyzing the Denominator:**\n   The denominator is \\(x^2 - 36x\\). We can factor it as \\(x(x - 36)\\). The critical points are \\(x = 0\\) and \\(x = 36\\).\n\n2. **Analyzing the Numerator:**\n   The numerator is \\(|x^2 - 81|\\). We can factor it as \\(|x^2 - 9^2|\\), which is \\(|x^2 - 9^2|\\). The critical points are \\(x = 9\\) and \\(x = -9\\).\n\n3. **Analyzing the Sign of the Denominator:**\n   - For \\(x < 0\\), \\(x^2 - 36x = x(x - 36)\\) is positive.\n   - For \\(0 < x < 36\\), \\(x^2 - 36x = x(x - 36)\\) is negative.\n   - For \\(x > 36\\), \\(x^2 - 36x = x(x - 36)\\) is positive.\n\n4. **Analyzing the Sign of the Numerator:**\n   - For \\(x < -9\\), \\(x^2 - 81\\) is positive.\n   - For \\(-9 < x < 9\\), \\(x^2 - 81\\) is negative.\n   - For \\(x > 9\\), \\(x^2 - 81\\) is positive.\n\n5. **Combining the Signs:**\n   - For \\(x < -9\\), the numerator is positive and the denominator is positive, so the fraction is positive.\n   - For \\(-9 < x < 9\\), the numerator is negative and the denominator is negative, so the fraction is positive.\n   - For \\(x > 9\\), the numerator is positive and the denominator is positive, so the fraction is positive.\n   - For \\(0 < x < 36\\), the numerator is negative and the denominator is negative, so the fraction is positive.\n   - For \\(x > 36\\), the numerator is positive and the denominator is positive, so the fraction is positive.\n\n6. **Finding the Fraction is Negative:**\n   - The fraction is negative only when the numerator is positive and the denominator is negative. This occurs in the interval \\(-9 < x < 9\\).\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is \\(\\boxed{-9 < x < 9}\\).",
