          "model_output": "To find the ratio of acceleration of Jen's ball to Jack's, we first need to determine the acceleration of each ball using the given formula: force = mass × acceleration.\n\nFor Jen's softball:\n- Mass = 200 g = 0.2 kg\n- Force = 200 g = 0.2 N\n- Acceleration = Force / Mass = 0.2 N / 0.2 kg = 1 m/s²\n\nFor Jack's baseball:\n- Mass = 150 g = 0.15 kg\n- Force = 150 g = 0.15 N\n- Acceleration = Force / Mass = 0.15 N / 0.15 kg = 1 m/s²\n\nNow, we can find the ratio of acceleration of Jen's ball to Jack's:\n- Ratio = Acceleration of Jen's ball / Acceleration of Jack's ball = 1 m/s² / 1 m/s² = 1\n\nTherefore, the ratio of acceleration of Jen's ball to Jack's is $\\boxed{1}$.",
