          "unique_id": "test/algebra/2743.json",
          "model_output": "Let's denote the cost of a pencil as \\( p \\) cents and the cost of a jumbo eraser as \\( j \\) cents. We are given two equations based on the problem statement:\n\n1. \\( 3p + j = 124 \\) (since three pencils and one jumbo eraser cost $1.24)\n2. \\( 5p + j = 182 \\) (since five pencils and one jumbo eraser cost $1.82)\n\nTo find the cost of a pencil, we need to eliminate \\( j \\) from these equations. We can do this by subtracting the first equation from the second equation:\n\n\\[\n(5p + j) - (3p + j) = 182 - 124\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the left side, we get:\n\n\\[\n5p + j - 3p - j = 2p\n\\]\n\nAnd simplifying the right side, we get:\n\n\\[\n182 - 124 = 58\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[\n2p = 58\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\( p \\), we divide both sides by 2:\n\n\\[\np = \\frac{58}{2} = 29\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of a pencil is $\\boxed{29}$ cents.",
          "model_answer": "29"
