          "model_output": "1. **Initial Setup**: We are given the recurrence relation:\n   \\[\n   f(n + 1) = (-1)^{n + 1} n - 2f(n)\n   \\]\n   for \\( n \\ge 1 \\).\n\n2. **First Step**: We need to find \\( f(1) \\).\n   \\[\n   f(2) = (-1)^{2} \\cdot 1 - 2f(1) = 1 - 2f(1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(3) = (-1)^{3} \\cdot 2 - 2f(2) = -2 - 2(1 - 2f(1)) = -2 - 2 + 4f(1) = -4 + 4f(1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(4) = (-1)^{4} \\cdot 3 - 2f(3) = 3 - 2(-4 + 4f(1)) = 3 + 8 - 8f(1) = 11 - 8f(1)\n   \\]\n\n3. **General Pattern**:\n   \\[\n   f(n) = (-1)^{n-1} (n-1) - 2f(n-1)\n   \\]\n   This pattern suggests that \\( f(n) \\) can be expressed as:\n   \\[\n   f(n) = (-1)^{n-1} (n-1) - 2f(n-1)\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solving the Recurrence**:\n   We solve the recurrence relation by expanding and simplifying:\n   \\[\n   f(n) = (-1)^{n-1} (n-1) - 2f(n-1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(n) = (-1)^{n-1} (n-1) - 2(-1)^{n-2} (n-2) + 2f(n-2)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(n) = (-1)^{n-1} (n-1) - 2(-1)^{n-2} (n-2) + 2(-1)^{n-3} (n-3) + \\dots + 2(-1)^2 (n-1) + 2f(1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(n) = (-1)^{n-1} (n-1) + 2f(1)\n   \\]\n\n5. **Summing the Series**:\n   We need to find the sum:\n   \\[\n   S = f(1) + f(2) + f(3) + \\dots + f(1985)\n   \\]\n   Using the formula for \\( f(n) \\):\n   \\[\n   S = \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} f(n) = \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-1)^{n-1} (n-1) + 2f(1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   S = \\sum_{n=1}^{1985} (-1)^{n-1} (n-1) + 2 \\cdot 1985\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   S = \\sum_{n=0}^{1984} (-1)^n n + 2 \\cdot 1985\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   S = \\sum_{n=0}^{1984} (-1)^n n + 3990\n   \\]\n\n6. **Evaluating the Sum**:\n   The sum of the series \\( \\sum_{n=0}^{1984} (-1)^n n \\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\sum_{n=0}^{1984} (-1)^n n = 0 - 1 + 2 - 3 + \\dots + 1984\n   \\]\n   This is an alternating series with the first term 0 and the last term 1984. The sum of an alternating series can be calculated as:\n   \\[\n   \\sum_{n=0}^{1984} (-1)^n n = \\frac{1984 \\cdot 1985}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\sum_{n=0}^{1984} (-1)^n n = \\frac{1984 \\cdot 1985}