          "unique_id": "test/algebra/2080.json",
          "model_output": "To simplify the given expression, we will use the distributive property to expand each product and then combine like terms.\n\nFirst, we expand $(u+4)(u-1)$:\n\\[\n(u+4)(u-1) = u(u-1) + 4(u-1) = u^2 - u + 4u - 4 = u^2 + 3u - 4\n\\]\n\nNext, we expand $(u-3)(u+6)$:\n\\[\n(u-3)(u+6) = u(u+6) - 3(u+6) = u^2 + 6u - 3u - 18 = u^2 + 3u - 18\n\\]\n\nNow, we subtract the second expanded expression from the first:\n\\[\n(u^2 + 3u - 4) - (u^2 + 3u - 18) = u^2 + 3u - 4 - u^2 - 3u + 18 = 14\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified expression is $\\boxed{14}$.",
