          "unique_id": "test/number_theory/679.json",
          "model_output": "First, we need to find the total amount of money Linda, Sherry, June, and Connie earned. We do this by adding their individual earnings:\n\n\\[\n27.47 + 35.23 + 37.37 + 26.52 = 135.68\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to convert this total amount into dollars and cents. Since there are 100 cents in a dollar, we divide the total by 100:\n\n\\[\n135.68 \\div 100 = 1.3668\n\\]\n\nThis means they can convert $1.3668$ dollars into bills. To find out how many bills they can make, we take the integer part of the division result, which is $1$. This means they can make $1$ bill.\n\nNow, we subtract the value of the bill from the total amount to find out how much money is left:\n\n\\[\n135.68 - 1 \\times 100 = 35.68\n\\]\n\nFinally, we convert the remaining amount into cents:\n\n\\[\n35.68 \\times 100 = 3568\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the amount of money left after they converted as many of the coins into bills as they could is $\\boxed{3568}$ cents.",
