          "problem": "Jim and Martha are standing together at the corner of a rectangular field. Jim walks diagonally across the field. Martha gets to the same location by walking along its length and width. The field is 300 feet wide and 400 feet long. How many feet less than Martha does Jim walk?",
          "solution": "The diagonal of the field is $\\sqrt{300^2+400^2}=500$ feet long so Jim walks 500 feet. Two adjacent sides of the field are $300+400=700$ feet long so Martha walks 700 feet. Jim walks $700-500=\\boxed{200}$ feet less than Martha.",
          "answer": "200",
          "subject": "Prealgebra",
          "level": 2,
          "unique_id": "test/prealgebra/1252.json",
          "model_output": "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the total distance Jim walks and then compare it to the distance Martha walks.\n\n1. **Calculate the diagonal distance Jim walks:**\n   Jim walks diagonally across the field, which forms a right triangle with the length and width of the field. We can use the Pythagorean theorem to find the diagonal distance.\n   \n   The Pythagorean theorem states that in a right triangle, the square of the length of the hypotenuse (the diagonal in this case) is equal to the sum of the squares of the lengths of the other two sides (the length and width of the field).\n   \n   Let's denote the length of the field as \\( L \\) and the width as \\( W \\).\n   \n   \\[\n   L = 400 \\text{ feet}, \\quad W = 300 \\text{ feet}\n   \\]\n   \n   The diagonal distance \\( d \\) can be calculated as:\n   \n   \\[\n   d = \\sqrt{L^2 + W^2}\n   \\]\n   \n   Substituting the given values:\n   \n   \\[\n   d = \\sqrt{400^2 + 300^2} = \\sqrt{160000 + 90000} = \\sqrt{250000} = 500 \\text{ feet}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the distance Martha walks:**\n   Martha walks along the length and width of the field. The total distance she walks is the sum of the length and the width.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Total distance Martha walks} = L + W = 400 + 300 = 700 \\text{ feet}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the difference in distance walked by Jim and Martha:**\n   To find out how many feet less Jim walks than Martha, we subtract the distance Jim walks from the distance Martha walks.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Difference in distance} = \\text{Distance Martha walks} - \\text{Distance Jim walks} = 700 - 500 = 200 \\text{ feet}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Jim walks \\(\\boxed{200}\\) feet less than Martha.",
          "model_answer": "200"
        },
