          "level": 3,
          "unique_id": "test/intermediate_algebra/1365.json",
          "model_output": "To find the minimum value of the function $f(x) = |x-p| + |x-15| + |x-p-15|$, we need to consider the different cases based on the value of $x$ relative to the points $p$, $15$, and $p+15$.\n\n1. **Case 1: $x < p$**\n   In this case, all three absolute value expressions can be simplified as:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = (p - x) + (15 - x) + (p + 15 - x) = 2p + 30 - 3x\n   \\]\n   Since $x < p$, the minimum value of $f(x)$ in this interval is achieved at $x = p$, giving:\n   \\[\n   f(p) = 2p + 30 - 3p = 30 - p\n   \\]\n\n2. **Case 2: $p \\leq x \\leq 15$**\n   In this interval, the absolute value expressions simplify as:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + (x - p - 15) = -2p - 2x\n   \\]\n   Since $p \\leq x \\leq 15$, the minimum value of $f(x)$ in this interval is achieved at $x = p$, giving:\n   \\[\n   f(p) = -2p - 2p = -4p\n   \\]\n\n3. **Case 3: $x > 15$**\n   In this interval, the absolute value expressions simplify as:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = (x - p) + (x - 15) + (x - p - 15) = 3x - 2p - 30\n   \\]\n   Since $x > 15$, the minimum value of $f(x)$ in this interval is achieved at $x = 15$, giving:\n   \\[\n   f(15) = 3(15) - 2p - 30 = 45 - 2p - 30 = 15 - 2p\n   \\]\n\nCombining the results from all cases, the minimum value of $f(x)$ for $x$ in the interval $p \\leq x \\leq 15$ is the minimum of $30 - p$, $-4p$, and $15 - 2p$.\n\n- When $p = 0$, the minimum value is $30 - 0 = 30$.\n- When $p = 15$, the minimum value is $15 - 2(15) = -15$.\n- When $0 < p < 15$, the minimum value is $15 - 2p$.\n\nTherefore, the minimum value taken by $f(x)$ for $x$ in the interval $p \\leq x \\leq 15$ is $\\boxed{15 - 2p}$.",
