          "model_output": "We start by expanding $(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3})^3$ using the binomial theorem:\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3})^3 = (\\sqrt{2})^3 + 3(\\sqrt{2})^2(\\sqrt{3}) + 3(\\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{3})^2 + (\\sqrt{3})^3\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2\\sqrt{2} + 3(2\\sqrt{2}) + 3(\\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{3})^2 + 3\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2\\sqrt{2} + 6\\sqrt{2} + 3\\sqrt{2} + 3\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\\[\n= 11\\sqrt{2} + 3\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\nThus, $a=11$, $b=3$, and $c=0$. Therefore, $a+b+c=11+3+0=\\boxed{14}$.",
