          "model_output": "1. **Identify the type of octagon**: The octagon is equiangular, meaning all interior angles are equal.\n\n2. **Calculate the interior angles**:\n   - The sum of the interior angles of an octagon is $(8-2) \\times 180^\\circ = 6 \\times 180^\\circ = 1080^\\circ$.\n   - Since it is equiangular, each interior angle is $\\frac{1080^\\circ}{8} = 135^\\circ$.\n\n3. **Determine the shape of the octagon**:\n   - The octagon can be divided into 8 isosceles triangles, each with a vertex angle of $135^\\circ$ and two sides of length $1$.\n   - The base of each triangle is the side of the octagon, which is either $1$ or $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\n\n4. **Calculate the area of one isosceles triangle**:\n   - The area of an isosceles triangle with two sides of length $1$ and an included angle of $135^\\circ$ is given by:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 1 \\times 1 \\times \\sin(135^\\circ) = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 1 \\times 1 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the total area of the octagon**:\n   - Since there are 8 such triangles, the total area of the octagon is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total Area} = 8 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} = 2\\sqrt{2}\n     \\]\n\nConclusion:\nThe area of the octagon is $\\boxed{2\\sqrt{2}}$.",
          "model_answer": "2\\sqrt{2}"
